@page "/about"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}
<h1>About this site</h1>
<p class="lede">
    <a href="https://linked.art/">Linked Art</a> is a community data model for describing art and cultural heritage, built on
    CIDOC-CRM and published as JSON-LD. <a href="https://github.com/tomcrane/linked-art-net">LinkedArtNet</a> is a .NET
    implementation of Linked Art 1.0: a typed model with a fluent API, a free-text date parser, a parsing service, and this site.
</p>

<h2>Why C#?</h2>
<p>
    JSON-LD examples are precise but hard to read in bulk. The same example as fluent C# reads like a description of the thing:
    a painting, produced by someone, at some time, carrying a title. Every example here is checked against the JSON that
    linked.art publishes, so the code you read is known to produce the real thing. Where it does not, the page says so and
    links the upstream issue.
</p>

<h2>Using the library</h2>
<p>Packages are not yet on NuGet; build from source. The repository README has the quick start. The libraries target .NET 10.</p>
